  "spacecraftVoyager1": "Launched in 1977. In 2012 it became the first spacecraft to enter interstellar space. Its radio signal is already about a day old when it reaches us.",
  "spacecraftVoyager2": "Launched in 1977. It is the only spacecraft that has visited Uranus and Neptune, and it entered interstellar space in 2018.",
  "spacecraftNewHorizons": "Flew past Pluto in 2015 and the Kuiper Belt object Arrokoth in 2019. It is still travelling outward and still sending data.",
  "spacecraftJwst": "The largest space telescope, launched in 2021. It sits near a point called L2, about 1.5 million km from Earth, with its sunshield always facing the Sun.",
