  "siteLuna9": "Luna 9 made the first soft landing on another world and sent back the first photos taken on the Moon's surface.",
  "siteSurveyor1": "Surveyor 1 was the first American soft landing on the Moon. It sent back more than 11,000 photos and showed that the ground was firm enough to land on.",
  "siteApollo11": "The first people on the Moon, Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin, landed here at Tranquility Base in July 1969.",
  "siteApollo12": "Apollo 12 landed close to the old probe Surveyor 3, and the crew brought some of its parts back to Earth.",
  "siteLuna16": "Luna 16 was the first robot to bring Moon soil back to Earth, about 100 grams, with no crew on board.",
  "siteLunokhod1": "Lunokhod 1 was the first rover on another world. It drove about 10 km over the Sea of Rains in eleven months.",
  "siteApollo14": "Apollo 14 landed in the Fra Mauro highlands. Alan Shepard hit two golf balls on the Moon.",
  "siteApollo15": "Apollo 15 was the first mission with a Moon buggy, and explored the foot of the Apennine mountains.",
  "siteApollo16": "Apollo 16 explored the Descartes highlands by rover and brought back about 95 kg of rocks.",
  "siteApollo17": "Apollo 17, in December 1972, is the most recent time people walked on the Moon. Geologist Harrison Schmitt was one of the two walkers.",
  "siteChange3": "China's Chang'e 3 put the Yutu rover on the Moon in December 2013, the first soft landing there since 1976.",
  "siteChange4": "Chang'e 4 made the first soft landing on the far side of the Moon, inside the huge South Pole-Aitken basin, in January 2019.",
  "siteChange5": "Chang'e 5 brought back about 1.7 kg of Moon samples in December 2020, the first new samples in 44 years.",
  "siteChandrayaan3": "India's Chandrayaan-3 landed near the Moon's south pole on 23 August 2023, making India the fourth country to land on the Moon.",
  "siteSlim": "Japan's SLIM landed in January 2024 within about 100 metres of its target, a very precise landing.",
  "siteViking1": "Viking 1 made the first successful Mars landing in July 1976 and worked on the surface for more than six years.",
  "siteViking2": "Viking 2 landed in Utopia Planitia in September 1976 and photographed frost on the red ground.",
  "sitePathfinder": "Mars Pathfinder landed in July 1997 and carried Sojourner, the first rover on Mars, about the size of a microwave oven.",
  "siteSpirit": "Spirit landed in Gusev crater in January 2004 and found signs that water once shaped the rocks there.",
  "siteOpportunity": "Opportunity landed in January 2004 and worked for almost 15 years, though it was built for 90 days.",
  "sitePhoenix": "Phoenix landed near the north pole in May 2008 and confirmed that there is water ice just under the soil.",
  "siteCuriosity": "Curiosity landed in Gale crater in August 2012 and showed that the place could once have supported microbial life.",
  "siteInsight": "InSight landed in November 2018 and recorded hundreds of marsquakes, listening to the inside of the planet.",
  "sitePerseverance": "Perseverance landed in Jezero crater in February 2021 with the helicopter Ingenuity, and collects rock samples for a future trip to Earth.",
  "siteZhurong": "China's Zhurong landed in May 2021, making China the second country to drive a rover on Mars.",
